  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "The composer has a cohesive cyber-defense visual language, crisp cyan/magenta semantics, a strong headline, and clear control-versus-result grouping. Desktop is polished and balanced. Tablet becomes very tall, while mobile is excessively dense and vertically protracted; numerous labels and annotations are tiny, and the two-column decision card feels cramped. The actual tablet/mobile header visibly clips the navigation mid-item, making it look unfinished. Header contrast also lacks proof: automated checks were incomplete for 14–26 nodes across viewports.",
    "fix": "Replace the clipped tablet/mobile header rail with an intentional compact navigation pattern; raise small-label contrast and minimum type size; reduce mobile vertical repetition by grouping paired controls more efficiently; and tighten the results hierarchy so the decision, risk score, evidence bars, and rationale scan as one concise outcome.",
